RAWKEYS(1)

# NAME

rawkeys - global keyboard policy authority for rawmkit

# SYNOPSIS

*rawkeys* [*-c* _FILE_] [*-C*] [*-v*]

# DESCRIPTION

*rawkeys* owns global X11 key grabs and routes admitted key chords to the
component that owns the requested mutation. Window-manager operations are sent
to rawm, panel and mixer operations are sent to rawpanel, and external programs
are started only from configured argv vectors.

rawkeys does not reconstruct window-manager state from EWMH. When per-window
XKB tracking is enabled it consumes focused-client identity from rawm's
published admitted-client inventory.

# OPTIONS

*-c* _FILE_
	Read one explicit configuration file instead of the normal system and user
	configuration cascade.

*-C*
	Validate configuration and exit without opening X11 or acquiring key grabs.

*-v*, *--version*
	Print the version and exit.

*-h*, *--help*
	Print usage and exit.

# LIFECYCLE

A running instance owns the per-screen selection
*\_RAWKEYS\_CONTROL\_Sn*. Its owner window publishes
*\_RAWKEYS\_CONTROL\_VERSION* with value 1. The selection is a singleton and
liveness boundary; version 0.1 defines no external mutation commands on it.

*SIGHUP* re-executes rawkeys with the original argv, releasing and reacquiring
all key grabs through normal X connection teardown. *SIGTERM* and *SIGINT*
terminate it.

# XKB POLICY

With *xkb.per\_window = true*, rawkeys stores the current XKB group on the
previous focused client and restores the stored group for the new focused
client. The state property is *\_RAWKEYS\_XKB\_GROUP* and belongs to rawkeys,
not rawm.

# SEE ALSO

*rawkeys.conf*(5), *rawm*(1), *rawpanel*(1), *rawctl*(1)
